      "care": "Thin crowded seedlings to 2–3 in. apart in damp weather or in the evening. Water dry soil first, firm afterwards and clear the thinnings to avoid attracting carrot fly.",
      "methods": [
        {
          "title": "Sow",
          "text": "Wait if the soil is cold or wet. Make shallow drills ½ in. deep and 6 in. apart, watering them first if dry. Sow very thinly; mixing the seed with dry sand can help. Cover with fine soil or compost and keep moist while the seeds germinate."
        },
        {
          "title": "Extend the season",
          "text": "Use short-rooted varieties for early or late crops. Early and later sowings need cloches or a sheltered spot."
        }
      ],
      "extended": "Early: Mar under cloches. Late: Aug; cover against frost.",
